"view.researchprojectdetailscreen.help"                     = "Here you see a summary of your research. The screen shows relevant choices from the configuration as well as some choices you already made. To run a research you must choose a file type and a data file. Enigma supports three formats: Standard Enigma, Gauquelin and QuickChart. More information about these formats can be found in the user manual. Use the 'Select file' button to select a data file on your disk. Make sure you have selected the correct file type.\n\nAfter selecting a file, Enigma shows how many records (horoscopes) the file contains.\n\nYou can now click the 'Start research' button.\n\nYou will then see an overview of the research results, both the regular data and the control group data. For large files a progress bar shows the progress. You can choose to stop the processing with the 'Interrupt' button.\n\nIf you used a control group multiplier greater than 1, you can display the average values. This makes the results of the real data and those of the control group easier to compare.\n\nAt the bottom of the data you see an 'Export to CSV…' button. This allows you to save the results in CSV format.";

